title: 'statement-store: hold a statement that has no routing target until a peer syncs it'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    On the v2 DHT path a node now keeps a statement that it cannot route. When the node is no
    replica for the statement's topics and has no connected peer closer to them, the statement
    stays held in the store until the initial sync of the next routing target delivers it.
    Before, the retention sweep removed such a statement and banned its hash, so a restart of
    the only routing peer toward a topic lost every statement sent in that window. The node
    holds at most 1024 such statements and counts the dropped ones under the `dead_end_full`
    reason of the undelivered statements metric.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
